    S(1, 2, "Inequalities", "If P > Q ≥ R = S < T, which of these is definitely true?",
      ["P > S", "Q > S", "T > Q", "S ≥ T"],
      "P > Q and Q ≥ R = S, so P > S. Q could equal S, the link between T and Q is unknown, and S < T rules out S ≥ T."),
    S(1, 3, "Coded relations", "'A + B' means A is the father of B, 'A x B' means A is the sister of B and 'A - B' means A is the wife of B. What does P - Q + R x S mean?",
      ["P is the mother of S", "P is the sister of S", "P is the aunt of S", "P is the grandmother of S"],
      "P is the wife of Q, Q is the father of R, and R is the sister of S. So Q is also S's father and his wife P is S's mother."),
    # ---------- Practice Test 2 ----------
    S(2, 1, "Blood relations", "Mohan is the only son of Ramesh. Ritu is the daughter-in-law of Ramesh. How is Ritu related to Mohan?",
      ["Wife", "Sister", "Cousin", "Sister-in-law"],
      "A daughter-in-law is a son's wife. Ramesh has only one son, Mohan, so Ritu must be Mohan's wife."),
